# agx: Relax pressure scheduler bail condition + set lload/lstore missing bit
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/42482 state=closed
# ### What does this MR do and why?

<!--Describe in detail what your merge request does and why.-->

This MR contains two performance optimizations for compute shaders, motivated by slow LLM inference on Asahi Linux using llama.cpp (see https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/10982).

1 relax pressure scheduler bail condition

Currently the pressure scheduler in the agx backend bails when compiling compute shaders (e.g. matrix multiplication) in llama.cpp's vulkan backend. This is due to the scheduler's reordered output having higher peak register pressure than its input. I found that when the scheduler is forced to never bail, prefill performance improves by around 18%. This patch relaxes the bail condition for compute shaders, allowing the pressure scheduler to produce code with higher register pressure than the original, as long as the higher pressure stays within the same workgroup occupancy tier.

2 set bit47 in lload/lstore instruction

When disassembling shader dumps compiled on macOS I always get `Unexpected set bits: [40, 47]` (see https://github.com/xingjianll/perf2/blob/main/metal/dumps/loop_lload_16/loop_lload_16.mesa.s), so these two bits appear to be set unconditionally in Metal emitted binaries. Bit 40 seems performance-unrelated, whereas setting bit 47 gives a sizeable performance improvement.

3 result

Running llama.cpp's standard perf harness gives the following results for prefilling (the speed at which llama.cpp processes the input prompt, measured in token/second, matmul bounded, higher is better) llama2-7B-Q4_0:

| current | bail relax | bail relax + bit47 |
|--------:|-----------:|-------------------:|
| 258.81 ± 0.99 | 305.32 ± 0.58 | 345.25 ± 0.54 |

My machine is M1 Ultra Mac Studio with 48-core GPU, and the program used for perf is llama.cpp on 1593d5684. The full llama.cpp vulkan backend test result that tests all of its compute shaders is in comparison.md.

